31-bit integers: the flags shifted in 63 bits.

bit63 shifted an int before making it an Int63: on wasm32 (31-bit ints),
bit 30 became min_int and bit 31 nothing, which Flags.Make refuses when
the module starts ("Flag.Make got flags with no bits set").

--- a/src/intel_cpuid.ml
+++ b/src/intel_cpuid.ml
@@
-let bit63 n = Int63.of_int (bit n)
+let bit63 n = Int63.shift_left Int63.one n
--- a/src/amd_cpuid.ml
+++ b/src/amd_cpuid.ml
@@
-let bit63 n = Int63.of_int (bit n)
+let bit63 n = Int63.shift_left Int63.one n
